          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Impact on Israel</strong><br>\nThe Yom Kippur War had far-reaching effects on Israel. It led to military and political introspection, and the Israeli government began to recognize the need for serious peace negotiations with its neighbors. It also led to an increase in the country's military readiness.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Arab States</strong><br>\nFor the Arab states, the war was both a military and a moral success. It improved the standing of Egypt and Syria in the Arab world and enabled them to gain a stronger negotiating position in later peace talks.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Long-term Consequences</strong><br>\nThe long-term consequences of the Yom Kippur War are still felt today. It helped set the stage for future peace agreements between Israel and its Arab neighbors. At the same time, the war also led to a permanent change in the regional military strategy and relations among the involved states.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
